      "review_title": "",
      "review_description": "For some reason the 20 x 310 watt Jinko panels were replaced with Jinko 18 x 360 watt  panels boosting the system from 6.2 kw to 6.4 kw.  It also makes it easier to add more panels if needed.  The company says the substitution was to \"ensure smoother operation of the system\" but I suspect it was really a stock in hand problem. No matter, I get the benefit.  The installation isn't fined as to come is still the inverter (A Fronius Sumo). The unit delivered was 5kw so It was sent back for the 6kw. The Fronius smart meter  is also yet to come.For your general info:  An Energy Australia representative told me that we could no longer change our tariff from ToU to a standard or fixed rate because the retailer would no longer do it.  Very odd.  The retailer told me that was \"rubbish\". Another Energy Australia representative (very cluey and obviously a higher rank) told me that it could be done but advised very strongly against it. It would cost us a lot more money.  Our recent bill is for $811 and we used less current that the same period 2017. The same period last year was $660.  My intention is to leave things the way we are and run with the solar system (when it is completed next week, hopefully) for one more quarter (for comparison reasons). After that, change to a fixed rate.   There's only two of us and we have solar hot water on a dedicated off-peak circuit.  I would like to say a big thank you too Solar Quote- for the invaluable knowledge and help.",
