      "overall_rating": 0,
      "review_title": "",
      "review_description": "Do not use this company for your solar installation if you wish to avoid delays, poor communication and sloppy administration. I received an initial estimate by email and this was followed up by a visit from a representative who was knowledgeable and informative. I was also informed that if I signed up before the end of November 2017 I would not come under the freedom of choice of installer that started on 1st December and that they could install the meter. This turned out to be untrue. Following the initial visit, all of my subsequent emails requesting information as to why installation was delayed, went unanswered.Their engineers showed me a roof plan but days before this it was changed apparently at the request of the installers. No effort was made to contact me to discuss this and as a result I have some unsightly panels on one roof.Installation was finally completed 3 months after I signed the contract but no reason was given. I then had to wait a further 3 months for the meter to be connected by Energy Australia. This may have taken longer had I not contacted Energy Ausralia myself to find that Powervault had given them a wrong telephone number, that they had been using to try and contact me regarding installation.I find it unacceptable that it should take 6 months to get a working solar system installed. This was responsible for me not saving on the cost of electricity during summer where generation is highest and the cost of running air conditioning and pool pumps the greatest.When I made my final payment I requested a receipt for this and some 6 weeks later I am still waiting to receive itThe only positive in the story was the quality of the service provided by the installers who did a great job and communicated well. Thanks to Nathan and Steve of Kraft Electrical Newcastle. I have used this company for subsequent unrelated electrical work",
